# Commit Message Pattern

Apply when the user asks to commit, amend, rebase commit messages, or push commits you authored.

## CRITICAL: No Cursor / AI attribution

Cursor may auto-inject `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` into commit messages. Treat every commit as suspect until verified clean.

### Never include

- `Made with Cursor` / `Made by Cursor`
- `Co-authored-by: Cursor` (or any AI/tool co-author trailer)
- `Generated by Cursor`, `AI-assisted`, or similar attribution

### After each commit (when you authored it)

Verify the message is clean:

```bash
git log -1 --format='%B' | grep -iE 'Co-authored-by:[[:space:]]*Cursor|Made (with|by) Cursor|Generated by Cursor'
```

Exit code must be 1 (no match). If it matches, amend:

```bash
git commit --amend -m "$(git log -1 --format=%s)"
```

Do not bypass hooks with `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>)?: <description>
```

- **type**: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `test`, `style`, `perf`
- **scope** (optional): feature area from the path (`plan`, `cost`, `skills`, `map`, `stores`, `scripts`)
- **description**: clear, concise summary in imperative mood

```
✅ GOOD
feat(plan): add pipeline checklist to plan detail
fix(cost): correct ME rounding for multi-run batches
test(manufacturingPlan): cover self-referencing blueprint chains

❌ BAD
feat: add stuff                    ← vague
Fixed bug                          ← no type prefix
feat(plan): add checklist

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

## Scope hints (this repo)

| Path | Scope |
|---|---|
| `src/lib/plan*.ts`, `src/components/plan/` | `plan` |
| `src/lib/cost.ts`, profit/ranking helpers | `cost` |
| `src/components/skills/`, skill lib | `skills` |
| `src/components/map/`, map lib | `map` |
| `src/stores/` | `stores` |
| `scripts/` | `scripts` |
| `.cursor/rules/` | `rules` |

## Commit body

Use a body only when the user asks for one or the change needs context. Default to title-only commits.

## Push

Only push when the user explicitly asks (PR workflow, "push", etc.). Otherwise stop after local commits.
